From f584de7cda116851a97b46f11ae422e443567603 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:41:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 26/37] drm/msm: bind ACPI display components with explicit
 resources and OPPs

The supplemental MDSS/DPU hierarchy has no OF component graph, clock
list or OPP table. It needs explicit resource, interrupt, component and
interconnect descriptions before KMS can run.

Match components by owned firmware-node references, obtain named clocks
and managed ICC paths, and validate the TCL MDSS/DPU resources against
their ACPI ancestor. Require the intended power domain and install the
SC7180 DPU catalog and dynamic performance-level OPPs. Include NULL-name
guards at the matching sites and synchronize/remove the MDSS IRQ domain
on teardown. GPU rendering and DSI/bridge initialization remain separate
parts of the graph.
